        move('the Sifrei 126:1 (read whole at the reading); 147:3-4 (reread whole — 17:1 by CALL when it comes); Bekhorot 37a:16-19, 37a:20-37b:5, 37b:7-8 (read whole at the docket); Mishnah Bekhorot 6:1-12 whole (read whole at the docket); cold_run_priesthood (CALL) — PR.acceptable(firstling_table) = %s, (beast_heads) = %s, (passing_blemish) = %s' % (V(PR_TABLE), V(PR_HEADS), V(PR_PASSING)), "LAME AND BLIND THE PARTICULARS THAT TEACH THE CLASS — 'any blemish' the general, 'lame or blind' the particulars, 'any ill blemish' the general again: what is like the particulars — EXPOSED AND NOT REGENERATING (126:1 — the Sifrei reads I8 in its own words: 'a particular singled out from the general to teach'; the Bavli reads I6 GENERAL-PARTICULAR-GENERAL at Bekhorot 37a:16-19, checked in MIDDOT.md — the hidden out by 'ill', the temporary out by reasoning and by the particulars' own choice 37a:20-37b:5; the measures 37b:7-8); THE LIST BY CALL to priesthood.acceptable's firstling table — 'one list serves the firstling (Deut 15:21 [IMPORT]) and Lev 27's redemption' (Mishnah Bekhorot 6:11-12's closing rule: slaughtered on the permanent blemishes, not on the passing, the old, the sick, the foul, the sinned-with, the killer, the doubtful sex); the six class heads of Leviticus 22:22 by CALL; the intended blemish barred (Mishnah 5:3): THE CELL'S VERDICT THE CLASS, never a list typed here")
        dat('THE PARAMETER the_blemish_class (by CALL — priesthood.acceptable(firstling_table); Mishnah Bekhorot 6 whole; 126:1 I8 / Bekhorot 37a I6 the two readings a DATA row); the exam\'s person the owner who slaughters the firstling on an exposed permanent blemish in his gates — accepted')
        return out("the blemish class (15:21) — 'any blemish, lame or blind, any ill blemish': exposed and not regenerating — the particulars teach the class (the Sifrei 126:1 I8; Bekhorot 37a:16-19 I6); the list by CALL to priesthood.acceptable's firstling table (Mishnah Bekhorot 6:11-12 — one list serves the firstling): THE PARAMETER the_blemish_class; the owner who slaughters the firstling on an exposed permanent blemish accepted", ['accepted'])
